{"resourceIdentifier":"1888","resourceName":"Larimer County Landfill Gas Flaring Project","description":"The Larimer County landfill is located in Larimer County, Colorado approximately 1 mile south of Fort Collins, Colorado. Prior to the project, the baseline activity was a landfill without a gas collection and destruction system. An active landfill gas collection system was voluntarily installed in September 2009 consisting of 41 wells. The gas is collected in a gathering system and piped to the landfill gas processing facility, where a blower sends the gas through a condensate sump and on to an open flare. GHG emission reductions occur when the methane in the landfill gas is destroyed in the flare and all the carbon in the methane (CH4) is converted to carbon dioxide (CO2), which has a much lower global warming potential.  PUBLIC COMMENT PERIOD: This project was open for public comment from 16 April – 16 May 2019.  No comments were received.","location":{"latitude":40.504000,"longitude":-105.125000},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1888"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CO"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3Degrees Group, Inc.."},{"type":"string","value":"Tamil Nadu, India"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1888"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"18637"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Methodology Under Development"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"GHD Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"23/12/2